 {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": ""}, {"time": "100", "text": "Fussy Kids Can Be Cured!<br/><br/>Many of us know the problem that many parents face when their kids spit out certain foods and turn down others.  Parents used to try all sorts of tactics to get their kids to try out new foods and clean up their plates. They would try waiting all night, hiding vegetables in food, arguing or giving rewards.", "id": 1, "image": ""}, {"time": "22500", "text": "Eventually, they would give in and let the child have whatever they wanted.  Now a compelling study in Wales has shown that these fussy children can be convinced to eat healthy foods by watching \"cool\" videos.", "id": 2, "image": ""}, {"time": "36500", "text": "In the study, children with fussy eating habits watched videos that showed role models enjoying and eating up the food that the fussy kids disliked. The role models were other children their own age who were sophisticated and \"cool.\" These cool kids ate healthy foods, ate them properly, and were praised for doing so.", "id": 3, "image": ""}, {"time": "58500", "text": "What the study found was that the fussy children changed their opinions about what they had to eat. Their eating habits also improved after they watched the video. Parents everywhere are thrilled!", "id": 4, "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn7le08ob06re2vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": [], "title": ""}]}]}